[profiles.guide]
notes = '''The right stick {rs} is a flick stick: push it to turn that way at once, then rotate it to keep turning. Gyro aims up, down and finely.
Gyro aims like the mouse. Hold {lb} and {rb} together to pause it while you reposition the controller, press {select} and {start} together to switch it off or on, and hold {l3} to recenter.
Rust uses Easy Anti-Cheat. The pad reaches the game as an ordinary keyboard and mouse, but the official servers don't run under Proton, and some community servers ban macros: this pack has none.
{west} uses and picks up; hold it for the options on a door, box or sleeping bag. {south} jumps, {east} crouches (a toggle) and {l3} sprints (a toggle).
{rt} attacks and {lt} aims or blocks; holding {lt} also slows the right stick for aiming. {rb} reloads.
Hold {lb} for the belt and pick a slot with the right stick {rs}. Pick the slot in your hand again to put it away. {left} and {right} step through the belt.
{north} opens the inventory; hold it for the crafting menu. In both, the right stick {rs} moves the cursor and {rt} clicks.
{up} is the flashlight or laser, hold {down} to talk. Hold {r3} to look around while running.
{select} lists the map, crafting, chat and the console. Hold {select} for the Flying mode (minicopter, scrap heli): {rt} climbs and {lt} drops. Hold {select} again to land back on foot.
Chat and the console need typing: {guide} + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard.'''

